@startuml
title Issue #4 - Create and Assign a Team Deliverable
hide footbox
skinparam shadowing false

actor "Project owner" as Owner
boundary "Deliverable board" as UI
control "Server Action" as Action
control "Team data-access layer" as Store
control "App authentication" as Auth
database "Payload" as Payload
database "Cloud Firestore" as Firestore

Owner -> UI: Enter title, description, assignee,\nand target deadline
UI -> Action: createDeliverable(projectId, input)
Action -> Auth: require authenticated app user
Auth -> Payload: Verify app-session JWT
Payload --> Auth: AppUser or unauthenticated
Auth --> Action: AppUser or null

alt unauthenticated
  Action --> UI: structured sign-in error
  UI --> Owner: Show error
else authenticated
  Action -> Action: Allowlist, validate, and normalize input
  Action -> Store: createProjectDeliverable(user, projectId, input)
  Store -> Firestore: Begin transaction; read project,\nowner membership, and assignee membership
  Firestore --> Store: Project and membership documents
  Store -> Firestore: Read optional parent chain
  Firestore --> Store: Parent documents
  Store -> Store: Check owner, membership, same-project parent,\nand dueAt <= finalDeadline - 72h

  alt invalid project, membership, parent, or deadline
    Store --> Action: Throw domain validation error
    Action --> UI: Structured error result
    UI --> Owner: Show error
  else valid
    Store -> Firestore: Write deliverable in transaction\n(status=open, timestamps, assignee snapshot)
    Firestore --> Store: Commit succeeds
    Store --> Action: Deliverable ID
    Action --> UI: Serializable success result
    UI -> Action: Reload project board
    Action -> Store: loadTeamProjectBoard(user, projectId)
    Store -> Firestore: Read project, members, deliverables
    Firestore --> Store: Board documents
    Store --> Action: TeamProjectBoard
    Action --> UI: Serializable board
    UI --> Owner: Display in assignee lane
  end
end
@enduml
